<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<RSLogix5000Content SchemaRevision="1.0" SoftwareRevision="16.03" TargetType="AddOnInstructionDefinition" ContainsContext="true" Owner="Dale Reed, Rockwell Automation" ExportDate="Fri Jul 31 10:46:33 2009" ExportOptions="References Context">
<Controller Use="Context" Name="ProcessObjix">
<DataTypes Use="Context">
<DataType Name="L_LINT_BOOL_ARRAY" Family="NoFamily" Class="User">
<Description>
<![CDATA[UDT containing a 64-bit (LINT-sized) BOOL array for use as a COP destination]]>
</Description>
<Members>
<Member Name="Bit" DataType="BOOL" Dimension="64" Radix="Decimal" Hidden="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Bit array]]>
</Description>
</Member>
</Members>
</DataType>
</DataTypes>
<AddOnInstructionDefinitions Use="Context">
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Use="Target" Name="L_OTE" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="00 Release" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="true" CreatedDate="2009-07-07T16:39:50.037Z" CreatedBy="Not Available" EditedDate="2009-07-31T14:46:17.129Z"
 EditedBy="Not Available" SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Output Energize (64-bit)]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Initial Release]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This instruction energizes the given Bit of the referenced LINT (64-bit integer)
tag, that is, it sets the given bit (true, 1) if the EnableIn condition is TRUE, or
clears the given bit (false, 0) if the EnableIn condition is FALSE.

If the given Bit number is outside the range 0..63, the controller will
MAJOR FAULT on an invalid array index (bad bit number). To keep
performance "snappy", there is no validity checking of the given Bit number!]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="Ref_LINT" DataType="LINT" Usage="InOut" Radix="Decimal" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[LINT in which to set/clear a bit]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Inp_BitNum" DataType="DINT" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Bit position to examine (0 .. 63)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Out" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Output (for visible animation)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Bit" DataType="L_LINT_BOOL_ARRAY">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Array of 64 BOOLs (must be in a UDT to COPy to it)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[If rung is false, clear selected bit and "Out"]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENABLE-IN FALSE LOGIC
============================================================
When EnableIn is false (false rung in LD, input of 0 in FBD),
CLEAR the given bit in the referenced LINT.

Procedure is the same as for EnableIn true, except we CLEAR the bit.
===================================================
CONVERT LINT TO BOOL [ array ]
===================================================
This COPy takes the input LINT and copies it into a BOOL array.
NOTE:  a BOOL array must be placed inside a UDT to do a COPy to it!!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[UID()COP(Ref_LINT,Wrk_Bit,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[===================================================
CLEAR THE GIVEN BIT IN THE ARRAY
===================================================
"Energize" the bit in the BOOL [ 64 ] array.
In this case, EnableIn is false, so the given bit is CLEARED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Wrk_Bit.Bit[Inp_BitNum])OTU(Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[===================================================
CONVERT UPDATED BOOL [ array ] BACK TO LINT
===================================================
This COPy takes the modified BOOL array and copies it
back into the Referenced LINT.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Wrk_Bit,Ref_LINT,1)UIE();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[If rung is true, set selected bit and "Out"]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
L_OTE : 64-bit Output Energize
============================================================
Revision 1.0-00 Release:  2009-Jun-31
Initial Release
============================================================
This instruction energizes the given Bit of the referenced LINT (64-bit integer)
output, that is, it sets the bit (true, 1) if the EnableIn condition is TRUE, or
clears the bit (false, 0) if the EnableIn condition is FALSE.

If the given Bit number is outside the range 0..63, the controller will
MAJOR FAULT on an invalid array index (bad bit number). To keep
performance "snappy", there is no validity checking of the given Bit number!

Logix (V16/V17) has a LINT data type, but bit instructions
(and AOI Input and Output Parameters) don't support LINT.

This version of the L_OTE instruction:

*  copies the referenced LINT into a 64-bit BOOL array
(This must be done with a UDT -- you can't COPy to
a BOOL array -- so there is a dependency on an
external type definition -- UDT!)

*  does NO checking of the bit number
(If the bit number is not in the range 0 to 63, the
controller will fault on an invalid array index!)

* energizes the appropriate bit in the array (to 1 or 0, depending
on the EnableIn state)

* copies the BOOL array back to the LINT reference

NOTE: to do this without copying over other references to
the LINT (say, in other Tasks), we must use a UID/UIE block!
===================================================
CONVERT LINT TO BOOL [ array ]
===================================================
This COPy takes the input LINT and copies it into a BOOL array.
NOTE:  a BOOL array must be placed inside a UDT to do a COPy to it!!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[UID()COP(Ref_LINT,Wrk_Bit,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[===================================================
ENERGIZE THE GIVEN BIT IN THE ARRAY
===================================================
Energize the bit in the BOOL [ 64 ] array.
In this case, EnableIn is true, so the given bit is SET.

NOTE: ON PRE-SCAN, THIS LOGIC IS SCANNED
FALSE, AND THE OTE WILL CAUSE THE BIT TO BE
TURNED OFF!  (Just like a normal OTE....)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(Wrk_Bit.Bit[Inp_BitNum])OTE(Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[===================================================
CONVERT UPDATED BOOL [ array ] BACK TO LINT
===================================================
This COPy takes the modified BOOL array and copies it
back into the Referenced LINT.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Wrk_Bit,Ref_LINT,1)UIE();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="L_LINT_BOOL_ARRAY"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
